WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.248
Steady daily effort beats bursts

2
00:00:02.248 --> 00:00:04.145
of talent followed by coasting.

3
00:00:04.145 --> 00:00:06.422
Here's the oldest proof we have.

4
00:00:07.672 --> 00:00:09.677
The hare was sure of his speed.

5
00:00:09.677 --> 00:00:11.968
The tortoise challenged him to a race anyway.

6
00:00:13.218 --> 00:00:15.414
The hare shot ahead, so far that

7
00:00:15.414 --> 00:00:17.610
the tortoise was barely moving behind him.

8
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:20.546
Sure of winning, he lay down

9
00:00:20.546 --> 00:00:22.231
under a tree for a nap.

10
00:00:22.231 --> 00:00:23.636
The tortoise just kept plodding.

11
00:00:24.886 --> 00:00:27.238
By the time the hare woke up and raced

12
00:00:27.238 --> 00:00:29.590
for the line, the tortoise was already crossing it.

13
00:00:31.886 --> 00:00:33.710
Slow and steady wins the race.

14
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:38.623
It plays out in languages, savings, fitness and business.

15
00:00:38.623 --> 00:00:41.471
Intense sprints followed by long breaks stall,

16
00:00:41.471 --> 00:00:44.320
while small daily steps keep adding up.

17
00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:47.438
You don't need to be the fastest.

18
00:00:47.438 --> 00:00:48.773
You need to keep going.

19
00:00:48.773 --> 00:00:50.641
And if you're the hare, don't let

20
00:00:50.641 --> 00:00:52.242
a head start make you complacent.

21
00:00:53.492 --> 00:00:55.748
Pick one goal and set a small

22
00:00:55.748 --> 00:00:58.004
daily minimum you can keep even on

23
00:00:58.004 --> 00:01:00.260
bad days, like ten minutes. Start today.
